{"type":"text","timestamp":1794651437633,"sessionID":"ses_e26711045ffehqquTcyhnlkCU0","part":{"id":"prt_1d98f8983001HmPPi12ShCFyjW","messageID":"msg_1d98f6f8e001jFYQpCr1SUiLQB","sessionID":"ses_e26711045ffehqquTcyhnlkCU0","type":"text","text":"Now I'll modify `cmd_check_anchors` to track attestation times and check pending proofs:\n","time":{"start":1794651425155,"end":1794651437632}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794651437648,"sessionID":"ses_e26711045ffehqquTcyhnlkCU0","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call-62555d80-a7ef-429a-84b1-c11bd4bfff87","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/record/record.py","newString":"def cmd_check_anchors(a):\n    \"\"\"Every anchor must be right, the writer's Sigstore ranges must cover entries 1..head with no gap or overlap,\n    and every range head must have its OpenTimestamps proof.\n    Checks every anchor even after a failure; exit 1 if anything was wrong, else 2 if anything couldn't be checked.\"\"\"\n    chain, _ = load_chain(a.ledger)\n    rows, bad, cant, ranges, stamped = [], [], [], [], set()\n    attestation_times = {}\n    ots_pending = set()\n    for path in _listdir(a.ledger, \"anchors\", ANCHOR_NAME, \"file in anchors\"):\n        n = os.path.basename(path)\n        m = ANCHOR_NAME.fullmatch(n)\n        seq = int(m.group(1))\n        if m.group(2) == \"ots\":\n            stamped.add(seq)\n        try:\n            if not 1 <= seq <= len(chain):\n                raise Bad(f\"anchors/{n}: no entry {seq}\")\n            raw = open(os.path.join(a.ledger, \"entries\", f\"{seq:06d}.json\"), \"rb\").read()\n            if m.group(2) == \"ots\":\n                t = check_ots(path, raw, a.explorer)\n                if t is None:\n                    ots_pending.add(seq)\n                rows.append({\"anchor\": n, \"kind\": \"opentimestamps\", \"existed_by\": iso(t) or \"pending\"})\n            else:\n                t, pred, commit = check_sigstore(path, chain[seq - 1][1], a.repo, a.workflow, a.ref)\n                if not isinstance(pred, dict) or not isinstance(pred.get(\"from_seq\"), int) or pred.get(\"to_seq\") != seq \\\n                        or not 1 <= pred[\"from_seq\"] <= seq or pred != range_predicate(chain, pred[\"from_seq\"], seq):\n                    raise Bad(f\"anchors/{n}: attested range {pred!r} doesn't match this chain\")\n                ranges.append((pred[\"from_seq\"], seq, commit))\n                attestation_times[seq] = t\n                rows.append({\"anchor\": n, \"kind\": \"sigstore\", \"entries\": f\"{pred['from_seq']}-{seq}\", \"existed_by\": iso(t),\n                             \"writer_commit\": commit})\n        except Bad as ex:\n            bad.append(str(ex))\n        except CantCheck as ex:\n            cant.append(f\"anchors/{n}: {ex}\")\n    for lo, hi, commit in sorted(ranges):\n        if hi not in stamped:\n            bad.append(f\"anchors/{hi:06d}.ots is missing, though the writer stamps every range head before attesting\")\n    if a.max_pending_hours is not None:\n        now = datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).timestamp()\n        for hi in attestation_times:\n            if hi in ots_pending:\n                hours_pending = int((now - attestation_times[hi]) // 3600)\n                if hours_pending > a.max_pending_hours:\n                    bad.append(f\"anchors/{hi:06d}.ots: still pending {hours_pending} h\")\n    covered, changes, prev_commit = 0, [], None","oldString":"def cmd_check_anchors(a):\n    \"\"\"Every anchor must be right, the writer's Sigstore ranges must cover entries 1..head with no gap or overlap,\n    and every range head must have its OpenTimestamps proof.\n    Checks every anchor even after a failure; exit 1 if anything was wrong, else 2 if anything couldn't be checked.\"\"\"\n    chain, _ = load_chain(a.ledger)\n    rows, bad, cant, ranges, stamped = [], [], [], [], set()\n    for path in _listdir(a.ledger, \"anchors\", ANCHOR_NAME, \"file in anchors\"):\n        n = os.path.basename(path)\n        m = ANCHOR_NAME.fullmatch(n)\n        seq = int(m.group(1))\n        if m.group(2) == \"ots\":\n            stamped.add(seq)\n        try:\n            if not 1 <= seq <= len(chain):\n                raise Bad(f\"anchors/{n}: no entry {seq}\")\n            raw = open(os.path.join(a.ledger, \"entries\", f\"{seq:06d}.json\"), \"rb\").read()\n            if m.group(2) == \"ots\":\n                t = check_ots(path, raw, a.explorer)\n                rows.append({\"anchor\": n, \"kind\": \"opentimestamps\", \"existed_by\": iso(t) or \"pending\"})\n            else:\n                t, pred, commit = check_sigstore(path, chain[seq - 1][1], a.repo, a.workflow, a.ref)\n                if not isinstance(pred, dict) or not isinstance(pred.get(\"from_seq\"), int) or pred.get(\"to_seq\") != seq \\\n                        or not 1 <= pred[\"from_seq\"] <= seq or pred != range_predicate(chain, pred[\"from_seq\"], seq):\n                    raise Bad(f\"anchors/{n}: attested range {pred!r} doesn't match this chain\")\n                ranges.append((pred[\"from_seq\"], seq, commit))\n                rows.append({\"anchor\": n, \"kind\": \"sigstore\", \"entries\": f\"{pred['from_seq']}-{seq}\", \"existed_by\": iso(t),\n                             \"writer_commit\": commit})\n        except Bad as ex:\n            bad.append(str(ex))\n        except CantCheck as ex:\n            cant.append(f\"anchors/{n}: {ex}\")\n    for lo, hi, commit in sorted(ranges):\n        # the writer stamps every range head before it attests, and a failed stamp stops the run: a missing proof\n        # was removed (found by Z, 2026-11-06)\n        if hi not in stamped:\n            bad.append(f\"anchors/{hi:06d}.ots is missing, though the writer stamps every range head before attesting\")\n    covered, changes, prev_commit = 0, [], None"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /workspace/record/record.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/record/record.py\n+++ /workspace/record/record.py\n@@ -385,8 +385,10 @@\n and every range head must have its OpenTimestamps proof.\n Checks every anchor even after a failure; exit 1 if anything was wrong, else 2 if anything couldn't be checked.\"\"\"\n chain, _ = load_chain(a.ledger)\n rows, bad, cant, ranges, stamped = [], [], [], [], set()\n+attestation_times = {}\n+ots_pending = set()\n for path in _listdir(a.ledger, \"anchors\", ANCHOR_NAME, \"file in anchors\"):\n     n = os.path.basename(path)\n     m = ANCHOR_NAME.fullmatch(n)\n     seq = int(m.group(1))\n@@ -397,26 +399,34 @@\n             raise Bad(f\"anchors/{n}: no entry {seq}\")\n         raw = open(os.path.join(a.ledger, \"entries\", f\"{seq:06d}.json\"), \"rb\").read()\n         if m.group(2) == \"ots\":\n             t = check_ots(path, raw, a.explorer)\n+            if t is None:\n+                ots_pending.add(seq)\n             rows.append({\"anchor\": n, \"kind\": \"opentimestamps\", \"existed_by\": iso(t) or \"pending\"})\n         else:\n             t, pred, commit = check_sigstore(path, chain[seq - 1][1], a.repo, a.workflow, a.ref)\n             if not isinstance(pred, dict) or not isinstance(pred.get(\"from_seq\"), int) or pred.get(\"to_seq\") != seq \\\n                     or not 1 <= pred[\"from_seq\"] <= seq or pred != range_predicate(chain, pred[\"from_seq\"], seq):\n                 raise Bad(f\"anchors/{n}: attested range {pred!r} doesn't match this chain\")\n             ranges.append((pred[\"from_seq\"], seq, commit))\n+            attestation_times[seq] = t\n             rows.append({\"anchor\": n, \"kind\": \"sigstore\", \"entries\": f\"{pred['from_seq']}-{seq}\", \"existed_by\": iso(t),\n                          \"writer_commit\": commit})\n     except Bad as ex:\n         bad.append(str(ex))\n     except CantCheck as ex:\n         cant.append(f\"anchors/{n}: {ex}\")\n for lo, hi, commit in sorted(ranges):\n-    # the writer stamps every range head before it attests, and a failed stamp stops the run: a missing proof\n-    # was removed (found by Z, 2026-11-06)\n     if hi not in stamped:\n         bad.append(f\"anchors/{hi:06d}.ots is missing, though the writer stamps every range head before attesting\")\n+if a.max_pending_hours is not None:\n+    now = datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).timestamp()\n+    for hi in attestation_times:\n+        if hi in ots_pending:\n+            hours_pending = int((now - attestation_times[hi]) // 3600)\n+            if hours_pending > a.max_pending_hours:\n+                bad.append(f\"anchors/{hi:06d}.ots: still pending {hours_pending} h\")\n covered, changes, prev_commit = 0, [], None\n for lo, hi, commit in sorted(ranges):\n     if lo != covered + 1:\n         bad.append(f\"the writer's ranges {'overlap' if lo <= covered else 'leave a gap'} at entry {min(lo, covered + 1)}\")\n","filediff":{"file":"/workspace/record/record.py","patch":"Index: /workspace/record/record.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/record/record.py\n+++ /workspace/record/record.py\n@@ -385,8 +385,10 @@\n and every range head must have its OpenTimestamps proof.\n Checks every anchor even after a failure; exit 1 if anything was wrong, else 2 if anything couldn't be checked.\"\"\"\n chain, _ = load_chain(a.ledger)\n rows, bad, cant, ranges, stamped = [], [], [], [], set()\n+attestation_times = {}\n+ots_pending = set()\n for path in _listdir(a.ledger, \"anchors\", ANCHOR_NAME, \"file in anchors\"):\n     n = os.path.basename(path)\n     m = ANCHOR_NAME.fullmatch(n)\n     seq = int(m.group(1))\n@@ -397,26 +399,34 @@\n             raise Bad(f\"anchors/{n}: no entry {seq}\")\n         raw = open(os.path.join(a.ledger, \"entries\", f\"{seq:06d}.json\"), \"rb\").read()\n         if m.group(2) == \"ots\":\n             t = check_ots(path, raw, a.explorer)\n+            if t is None:\n+                ots_pending.add(seq)\n             rows.append({\"anchor\": n, \"kind\": \"opentimestamps\", \"existed_by\": iso(t) or \"pending\"})\n         else:\n             t, pred, commit = check_sigstore(path, chain[seq - 1][1], a.repo, a.workflow, a.ref)\n             if not isinstance(pred, dict) or not isinstance(pred.get(\"from_seq\"), int) or pred.get(\"to_seq\") != seq \\\n                     or not 1 <= pred[\"from_seq\"] <= seq or pred != range_predicate(chain, pred[\"from_seq\"], seq):\n                 raise Bad(f\"anchors/{n}: attested range {pred!r} doesn't match this chain\")\n             ranges.append((pred[\"from_seq\"], seq, commit))\n+            attestation_times[seq] = t\n             rows.append({\"anchor\": n, \"kind\": \"sigstore\", \"entries\": f\"{pred['from_seq']}-{seq}\", \"existed_by\": iso(t),\n                          \"writer_commit\": commit})\n     except Bad as ex:\n         bad.append(str(ex))\n     except CantCheck as ex:\n         cant.append(f\"anchors/{n}: {ex}\")\n for lo, hi, commit in sorted(ranges):\n-    # the writer stamps every range head before it attests, and a failed stamp stops the run: a missing proof\n-    # was removed (found by Z, 2026-11-06)\n     if hi not in stamped:\n         bad.append(f\"anchors/{hi:06d}.ots is missing, though the writer stamps every range head before attesting\")\n+if a.max_pending_hours is not None:\n+    now = datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).timestamp()\n+    for hi in attestation_times:\n+        if hi in ots_pending:\n+            hours_pending = int((now - attestation_times[hi]) // 3600)\n+            if hours_pending > a.max_pending_hours:\n+                bad.append(f\"anchors/{hi:06d}.ots: still pending {hours_pending} h\")\n covered, changes, prev_commit = 0, [], None\n for lo, hi, commit in sorted(ranges):\n     if lo != covered + 1:\n         bad.append(f\"the writer's ranges {'overlap' if lo <= covered else 'leave a gap'} at entry {min(lo, covered + 1)}\")\n","additions":12,"deletions":2},"truncated":false},"title":"workspace/record/record.py","time":{"start":1794651437630,"end":1794651437638}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now I need to modify `cmd_check_anchors` to:\n1. Track the attestation time (integrated_time `t`) for each range head (which is `seq` in the sigstore case, i.e., `hi`)\n2. After checking all anchors, for each range head, check if its OTS proof is pending and if the attestation time is older than max_pending_hours\n\nThe key insight is:\n- When processing sigstore anchors, we get `t` (integrated_time) and `seq` (which is the range head `hi`)\n- When processing OTS anchors, we check the proof and get a timestamp or `None` if pending\n- We need to correlate these: for each range head `hi`, we need to know its attestation time `t` from the sigstore anchor, and then check if the OTS proof for `hi` is pending\n\nLet me restructure the code:\n1. Create a dict `attestation_times` mapping range head (hi) -> attestation time (t)\n2. Create a dict `ots_status` mapping seq -> (timestamp or None for pending)\n3. After processing all anchors, for each range head in `attestation_times`, check if its OTS proof is pending and if so, check the time difference\n\nActually, looking at the code more carefully:\n- `ranges` contains tuples of `(from_seq, to_seq, commit)` where `to_seq` is the range head `hi`\n- `stamped` contains the set of seqs that have .ots files\n- But we don't currently track which OTS proof corresponds to which range head's attestation time\n\nLet me think about this differently. The sigstore attestation for a range head `hi` gives us the attestation time `t`. The OTS proof for that same `hi` is checked separately. We need to:\n1. Store attestation time for each range head when processing sigstore anchors\n2. Store OTS proof status (timestamp or pending) for each seq when processing OTS anchors\n3. After processing, for each range head, check if its OTS is pending and attestation time is old enough\n\nLet me modify the code to do this.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_1d98fba3b001tzg4ut6QqmFwOs","sessionID":"ses_e26711045ffehqquTcyhnlkCU0","messageID":"msg_1d98f6f8e001jFYQpCr1SUiLQB"}}
