{"type":"text","timestamp":1794651472922,"sessionID":"ses_e26711045ffehqquTcyhnlkCU0","part":{"id":"prt_1d9903d34001u4xYJ5D0HqA1pR","messageID":"msg_1d9902c25001ZIduC5RHD0bL4K","sessionID":"ses_e26711045ffehqquTcyhnlkCU0","type":"text","text":"All tests pass. The implementation is complete.\n\n**Summary of changes:**\n\n1. Added `--max-pending-hours H` argument to the `check-anchors` command parser in `main()`\n\n2. Modified `cmd_check_anchors()` to:\n   - Track `attestation_times` dict mapping range head seq → sigstore integrated_time\n   - Track `ots_pending` set of seqs with pending OTS proofs\n   - When `--max-pending-hours` is provided, check each range head: if its OTS is pending and attestation time is > H hours ago, add error \"anchors/NNNNNN.ots: still pending N h\" and exit 1\n\nThe behavior:\n- Without `--max-pending-hours`: pending proofs accepted (exit 0) — unchanged\n- With `--max-pending-hours H`: exit 1 if any range head's proof is pending and its attestation is > H hours old, printing \"still pending N h\" to stderr\n- Pending proof younger than H hours: exit 0","time":{"start":1794651471156,"end":1794651472912}}}
